WithAsync enables async mode. The callback is invoked in a goroutine
when the operation completes with either the result or an error.

Usage:

	// Synchronous (default)
	msg, err := mgr.SendTextMessage(ctx, req)

	// Asynchronous
	mgr.SendTextMessage(ctx, req, manager.WithAsync(func(result interface{}, err error) {
	    msg := result.(*model.Message)
	    // handle result or error
	}))

DescribeCreditUsageInfo retrieves credit usage information.
Supports both sync and async modes via CallOption.

Sync usage:

	info, err := mgr.DescribeCreditUsageInfo(ctx, &manager.DescribeCreditUsageInfoRequest{UsageType: "agent"})

Async usage:

	mgr.DescribeCreditUsageInfo(ctx, req, manager.WithAsync(func(result interface{}, err error) {
	    info := result.(*model.CreditUsageInfo)
	    // handle result or error
	}))

GenerateSceneUrl generates a scene URL for the specified desktop.
Supports both sync and async modes via CallOption.

Sync usage:

	resp, err := mgr.GenerateSceneUrl(ctx, &manager.GenerateSceneUrlRequest{
	    DesktopId: agent.RuntimeResourceInfo.ResourceId,
	    Scene:     "app-0a9mg1hbum7mueze1",
	})

Async usage:

	mgr.GenerateSceneUrl(ctx, req, manager.WithAsync(func(result interface{}, err error) {
	    resp := result.(*GenerateSceneUrlResponse)
	    // handle result or error
	}))

UpdateAgentInstance updates the metadata of an existing agent instance.
Supports both sync and async modes via CallOption.

Sync usage:

	err := mgr.UpdateAgentInstance(ctx, &manager.UpdateAgentInstanceRequest{
	    AgentInstanceId:   "agent-123",
	    AgentInstanceName: "New Name",
	})

Async usage:

	mgr.UpdateAgentInstance(ctx, req, manager.WithAsync(func(result interface{}, err error) {
	    // handle result or error
	}))

EntUninstallSkills uninstalls skills for the enterprise and waits for all operations to complete.
It returns the final operation task results after polling.

Sync usage:

	tasks, err := mgr.EntUninstallSkills(ctx, &manager.EntUninstallSkillsRequest{
	    SkillInfos: []model.UninstallSkillInfo{{SkillID: "skill-1", SkillName: "name-1"}},
	})

Async usage:

	mgr.EntUninstallSkills(ctx, req, manager.WithAsync(func(result interface{}, err error) {
	    tasks := result.([]*model.OperationTask)
	}))
